WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.580
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉您的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.170
Oh, boy.
天哪。

9
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.410
It's a big one today.
今天这集很重要。

10
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.470
That's what she said.
她也是这么说的。

11
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.510
I mean, I didn't even say hello.
我是说，我甚至还没打招呼呢。

12
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:33.370
Hello.
你好。

13
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.010
Say hello.
打个招呼吧。

14
00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:36.830
FirSt.
首先。

15
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:44.890
I mean, I'm just thinking about everything we have to share about Niagara, the wedding episode.
我是说，我一直在想关于婚礼那集《尼亚加拉》我们有多少内容要分享。

16
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.250
The enormous two-parter.
那可是个宏大的上下集。

17
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.970
We're doing it in two parts.
我们要分两部分来聊。

18
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:50.930
This is so big.
这太重要了。

19
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:51.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

20
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.090
Today is Niagara Part 1.
今天是《尼亚加拉》第一部分。

21
00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.690
It was Season 6, Episode 4.
这是第六季第四集。

22
00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:03.170
It was written by Greg Daniels and Mindy Kaling and directed by Paul Feig.
由格雷格·丹尼尔斯和敏迪·卡灵编剧，保罗·费格执导。

23
00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.490
I mean, we brought out the heavy hitters for this one.
我是说，我们为了这一集请出了重量级人物。

24
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.550
We sure did.
确实如此。

25
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.590
And we have a heavy hitter today on Office Ladies.
今天在《办公室》女士节目中，我们也请到了一位重量级嘉宾。

26
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.390
We sure do, guys.
没错，伙计们。

27
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:22.630
Co-writer of this episode and showrunner of The Office, Greg Daniels, has come on Office Ladies to discuss this epic milestone episode.
本集编剧之一、《办公室》剧集主管格雷格·丹尼尔斯来到了《办公室》女士节目，与我们讨论这一史诗般的里程碑剧集。

28
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.470
We could not be more excited.
我们激动得不得了。

29
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.570
We are thrilled.
我们太兴奋了。

30
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.370
Let's talk to Greg.
让我们和格雷格聊聊吧。

31
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.960
Greg Daniels!
格雷格·丹尼尔斯！

32
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:33.480
Hello!
你好！

33
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:34.800
Hey!
嘿！

34
00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:35.820
Welcome!
欢迎！

35
00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.500
This is a huge treat!
这真是太难得了！

36
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.020
We are so excited to have you on Office Ladies.
能请你来《办公室》女士节目，我们太激动了。

37
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:40.940
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

38
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.600
For me, too.
我也是。

39
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:42.860
It's so nice to see you guys.
见到你们真好。

40
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.060
And this is a milestone episode.
这一集确实是一个里程碑。

41
00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:45.820
Big one.
非常重要的一集。

42
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:46.720
Very big one.
非常非常重要。

43
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:53.580
Jen and I were saying, just prepping our document for this week's record, we felt like we were building like a small airplane.
珍和我说，在准备这周录音的文档时，感觉就像在造一架小型飞机。

44
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:59.260
Because there was like so many different stories and articles and DVD commentaries.
因为有太多不同的故事、文章和DVD评论音轨了。

45
00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.560
And we're just so glad you're here and we get to break it down with you.
我们很高兴你能来，能和你一起剖析这一集。

46
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:08.520
I went back into the archives, you know, and looked at some of our notes from the writer's room.
我翻回了档案，你知道的，看了看我们编剧室的一些笔记。

47
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:15.800
And, you know, I realized that we had gamed this one so thoroughly from the beginning.
然后，我意识到我们从一开始就把这一集构思得非常透彻。

48
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.180
This was like my special point of the season, obviously.
显然，这是我这一季的重点。

49
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.220
This was like the biggest moment that we had.
这是我们当时最重要的时刻。

50
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.900
So we had really put a lot of effort and thought into it.
所以我们确实在上面投入了大量的精力和思考。

51
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.920
Randy Cordray told us that before Season 6 even started, you told him,
兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，在第六季还没开始之前，你就跟他说过，

52
00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.700
Pam and Jim are going to get married on The Maid of the MiSt.
“吉姆和帕姆要在‘雾中少女号’上结婚。”

53
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.480
Figure that out.
“去把这事儿搞定。”

54
00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:33.680
Yeah.
没错。

55
00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:34.120
Yeah.
没错。

56
00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:42.280
So this was a crazy year for me, personally, because this was the first year that I had an official co-showrunner in Paul Lieberstein.
所以对我个人而言，这是疯狂的一年，因为这是我第一次有保罗·利伯斯坦作为正式的联合剧集主管。

57
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:50.040
You know, and I was also running Season 2 of Parks and Rec at the same time as Season 6 of The Office with Mike Schur.
你知道，当时我还在和迈克·舒尔一起负责《公园与游憩》第二季，同时还要忙《办公室》第六季。

58
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:56.200
And there was, we had like the biggest, juiciest writing staff possible.
而且我们当时拥有最庞大、最给力的编剧团队。

59
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.760
Like this was one of our classic years writing staff.
那绝对是我们编剧团队的巅峰时期之一。

60
00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.440
Everybody was great.
每个人都很棒。

61
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.480
So there was a lot of help.
所以得到了很多帮助。

62
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.120
But I think I did 50 episodes this year.
但我估计我那年做了50集节目。

63
00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

64
00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:15.780
Between the two shows, which is like 50 table readings, 50 script locks, 50 production meetings, 50 cuts having to be locked.
两部剧加起来，意味着50次剧本围读，50次剧本定稿，50次制作会议，50次剪辑定剪。

65
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.420
So I was like super crazed for this year.
所以我那年简直忙疯了。

66
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.360
And the things that I really wanted to concentrate on for The Office was Jim and Pam's wedding,
而我真正想在《办公室》里专注的事情就是吉姆和帕姆的婚礼，

67
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.660
because I felt like this was the culmination of a six-year story that was so important to the show.
因为我觉得这是六年来故事的高潮，对这部剧来说非常重要。

68
00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.120
And so we put a lot of brain work into it.
所以我们在这上面投入了大量的心血。

69
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:46.260
And with the Niagara part, that was like what I had sort of figured out for the wedding, because the wedding had to be filled with comedy for all of the side characters.
至于尼亚加拉大瀑布的部分，那是我为婚礼构思好的，因为婚礼必须充满喜剧元素，要照顾到所有的配角。

70
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.660
But it also had to be very romantic for Jim and Pam.
但对吉姆和帕姆来说，它也必须非常浪漫。

71
00:03:51.020 --> 00:04:00.940
And the show always had this slight anomaly that was Jim and Pam, because it was so fairytale inside their relationship.
这部剧一直有一个小小的反差，那就是吉姆和帕姆，因为他们的关系简直像童话一样。

72
00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:06.760
But then everything else in the show was up for grabs for jokes and, you know, was very realistic.
但剧中的其他一切都可以拿来开玩笑，你知道，非常写实。

73
00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:14.520
And Niagara Falls is within a drive, like a conceivable four and a half hour drive of Scranton.
而且从斯克兰顿开车去尼亚加拉大瀑布，大概只需要四个半小时，完全在可接受范围内。

74
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:23.120
And so it made sense that you could invite people from work and they would drive up, you know, and it was a doable thing.
所以邀请同事们去参加，他们开车过去，这完全是可行的。

75
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.840
And so I did a lot of research on Niagara Falls way early.
所以我很早就对尼亚加拉大瀑布做了很多研究。

76
00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:37.780
And what's amazing about Niagara Falls, it's like the most classic wedding location for people, you know, in the NortheaSt.
尼亚加拉大瀑布最神奇的地方在于，它是美国东北部人们最经典的婚礼举办地，你知道的。

77
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:42.440
And it's been that way since the 1800s or whenever it was discovered.
从19世纪或者它被发现以来一直都是这样。

78
00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:50.660
And it's it's incredibly naturally beautiful and and like take your breath away, majestic.
它自然景观极其壮丽，美得让人窒息。

79
00:04:50.660 --> 00:05:02.400
But because everybody used it as their wedding thing, there was this really kind of commercialized, like kitschy industry that had developed around it.
但因为每个人都把它当作婚礼首选地，所以围绕它发展出了一种非常商业化、甚至有点俗气的产业。

80
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.160
So it was like a great location because you could have, you know,
所以这是一个很棒的地点，因为你可以，你知道，

81
00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:16.100
for the the one sort of thing we had going into it was this idea that I don't know if you were ever told this on on your guys's weddings.
我们当时有一个想法，不知道你们在自己的婚礼上有没有听过这种话。

82
00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:21.700
But, you know, they always say, like, the wedding is for your family and the marriage is what you get.
人们总是说，婚礼是办给家人看的，而婚姻才是你真正得到的。

83
00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:28.820
And so there's this sense of like the wedding's this public event and you have to invite your family and all these different people.
所以有一种感觉，婚礼是一场公开活动，你必须邀请家人和各种各样的人。

84
00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:33.240
And it's not always exactly what you wanted, but at least you get the marriage.
虽然不一定完全如你所愿，但至少你得到了婚姻。

85
00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:33.500
Right.
没错。

86
00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.060
So I think there was this going into the episode,
所以我觉得在构思这一集的时候，

87
00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:44.660
there was going to be this sort of two things happening where Pam and Jim wanted to have something that was beautiful and romantic for the two of them.
会有两件事同时发生：帕姆和吉姆想要一场属于他们两人的、美丽而浪漫的婚礼。

88
00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:53.380
But they also had to, you know, they had all these obligations with their family and the people from work and that was going to have all these people there.
但他们也必须面对现实，他们有来自家庭和同事的各种义务，所以会有很多人出席。

89
00:05:53.740 --> 00:06:04.880
So there was this contrast between like the comedy of having all their relatives and, you know, Pam's mother was upset, you know, and her parents had gotten divorced.
因此，喜剧效果与现实压力之间形成了对比，比如所有的亲戚都来了，帕姆的妈妈很不高兴，而且她父母已经离婚了。

90
00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:11.140
And, you know, the fact that Pam was pregnant and kind of hiding it, like there are all these different storylines happening for comedy.
还有，帕姆怀孕了却在隐瞒，所有这些不同的情节线都带来了喜剧效果。

91
00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:15.860
And Greg, I love that it was the destination wedding because on the commentary,
格雷格，我喜欢这是场目的地婚礼，因为在评论音轨里，

92
00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:25.420
you were saying a lot of different elements of this episode were based on real life things in the writer's room, like the destination wedding that you think no one will come to,
你说过这一集的很多元素都取材于编剧室里的真实经历，比如你以为没人会来的目的地婚礼，

93
00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:26.980
but then a lot of people show up.
结果却有很多人出席。

94
00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:27.440
Yeah.
没错。

95
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:40.040
And then there was like, there was a moment that I pulled from a friend of mine's wedding story where I guess his sister by mistake broke one of the wedding gifts,
还有一个情节是我从朋友的婚礼故事里借用的，他妹妹不小心弄坏了一件结婚礼物，

96
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.540
which was like a set of plates or something like that, that they had registered for.
好像是一套他们登记索要的盘子之类的东西。

97
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.880
And she was super upset about it.
她当时难过极了。

98
00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:57.040
And my friend couldn't really calm her down until he took one of the other plates and smashed it in front of her and said, look, this is not about the plates.
我朋友怎么劝都劝不住，直到他拿起另一个盘子当场摔碎，对她说：看，这根本不是盘子的问题。

99
00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.900
This is, I want you to, you know, enjoy my wedding.
我只是希望你能享受我的婚礼。

100
00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:07.660
And so that, that kind of translated into Jim cutting his tie to make Pam feel better.
所以，这转化成了吉姆剪断领带去安慰帕姆的情节。

101
00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.720
That is such a cool moment.
那一刻真是太酷了。

102
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:10.740
Yeah.
是啊。

103
00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.560
I love that moment.
我喜欢那一刻。

104
00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:11.940
Yeah.
是啊。

105
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.760
I, I, I teared up.
我，我，我当时都看哭了。

106
00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:20.160
I, you know, there were so many wonderful moments that I had just forgotten about, about this episode.
你知道，这一集里有太多精彩的瞬间，我都快忘了。

107
00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.640
I think when I think of this episode too, I always think about the big wedding moment.
我觉得当我想到这一集时，我总是会想到那场盛大的婚礼时刻。

108
00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.300
I completely forgot about the cold open.
我完全忘了开场戏了。

109
00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:26.600
Yeah.
是啊。

110
00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.140
Oh yeah.
噢，没错。

111
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:37.980
A dozen people puking to open up the romantic wedding episode.
在一场浪漫的婚礼开篇，竟然有十几个人在呕吐。

112
00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:38.840
Yeah.
是啊。

113
00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.940
Well, I mean, that was the thing, right?
嗯，我的意思是，重点就在这儿，对吧？

114
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:45.920
It's like, we had so many cards on the board for ideas.
就像是，我们在白板上列了好多点子。

115
00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:51.380
You know, for the season and for this important, you know, episode.
你知道，为了这一季，也为了这一集重要的内容。

116
00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:59.060
And this was also a two part episode, which meant that there had to be like six acts of, of story.
而且这还是上下两集，意味着必须要有六幕的剧情。

117
00:07:59.320 --> 00:07:59.480
Right.
没错。

118
00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.760
So, and a lot of different people did, they didn't have their own subplot.
所以，很多人并没有属于他们自己的支线剧情。

119
00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.160
You know, it wasn't like, Oh, well, don't worry.
你知道，不像那种，噢，别担心。

120
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:11.360
Andy and Michael are having a subplot where they're selling to some, you know, they're there at the wedding.
安迪和迈克尔有条支线，他们在卖东西，或者你知道，他们就在婚礼现场。

121
00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.120
So they all have to have their own comedy stories.
所以他们每个人都必须有自己的喜剧故事。

122
00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:22.720
So we generated in the writer's room, you know, just hundreds of cards of funny things that could happen.
我们在编剧室里构思了成百上千张卡片，写满了可能发生的趣事。

123
00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:31.120
And then we had to kind of jam them all, you know, into the, the, the overall feeling of, of a destination wedding in Niagara.
然后我们得把它们一股脑儿地塞进尼亚加拉大瀑布目的地婚礼的整体氛围里。

124
00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:38.060
That was the whole thing about the episode was balancing how much comedy to put in and how much romance and good feeling to put in.
这一集的关键就在于平衡喜剧成分与浪漫温馨的氛围。

125
00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:45.260
Well, one of my favorite things is this agreement that everyone's going to keep Pam's pregnancy a secret from Meemaw.
嗯，我最喜欢的情节之一就是大家达成共识，要对米玛保密帕姆怀孕的事。

126
00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.360
We're not going to tell Meemaw.
我们不能告诉米玛。

127
00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.600
Like what a disaster already, right?
这简直是一场灾难，对吧？

128
00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.260
That Michael's not going to be able to keep the secret.
迈克尔肯定守不住这个秘密。

129
00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.580
We all think Michael's going to spill the beans.
我们都觉得迈克尔会说漏嘴。

130
00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.260
Well, first of all, I have a question about the name Meemaw.
嗯，首先，我对“米玛”这个称呼有个疑问。

131
00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.160
Is that, was that based on someone's real life?
这是基于现实生活中的某个人吗？

132
00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.360
I had never heard that.
我以前从没听说过。

133
00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:10.620
I've heard like Grammy, Gigi as names for grandmas, but Meemaw was new to me.
我听过奶奶叫“格莱美”或“吉吉”，但“米玛”对我来说很新鲜。

134
00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:11.980
Is that an East Coast thing?
这是东海岸的叫法吗？

135
00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:12.900
I don't think so.
我不这么认为。

136
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.560
I think that's like a pioneer thing.
我觉得那更像是老派的叫法。

137
00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.960
Personally, I kind of feel like that's a.
我个人觉得那是……

138
00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.340
I've heard of Meemaw.
我听说过米玛。

139
00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:19.340
Is it Southern?
是南方的叫法吗？

140
00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:27.180
I think it might be Southern or I think like what Greg's saying, kind of like ye olde pioneer days, but my dad was called Pawpaw.
我觉得可能是南方的，或者像格雷格说的那样，是那种古老的先驱时代的叫法，但我爸爸以前被称为“波波”。

141
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.280
Yeah.
是啊。

142
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.660
We might've gotten it from you.
我们可能是从你那儿听来的。

143
00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.920
Did you have a Meemaw?
你有过米玛吗？

144
00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:37.200
I didn't have a Meemaw, but it's certainly like when I read it, I was like, sure, you're Meemaw.
我没有米玛，但当我读到这个词时，我确实觉得，嗯，你就是米玛。

145
00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.520
Like it's in my brain somewhere.
就像它存在于我脑海里的某个地方一样。

146
00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:46.020
Well, I mean, the idea was that she was pretty old fashioned person who was going to be, you know, pretty judgmental.
嗯，我的意思是，这个角色的设定是一个非常守旧、而且会很爱评头论足的人。

147
00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:49.140
And the actress was kind of amazing.
那位演员真是太棒了。

148
00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:53.100
Like she started in Westerns in the 1930s, that actress, Peggy Stewart.
那位演员佩吉·斯图尔特，她从20世纪30年代就开始演西部片了。

149
00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:58.220
And so she, she, I think was a, was a Meemaw.
所以她，我觉得她就是个米玛。

150
00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:11.320
Well, it ends up being Jim in just a brilliant piece of writing and performance then by John Krasinski, who ends up spilling the beans.
结果最后是吉姆说漏了嘴，这真是约翰·卡拉辛斯基在剧本创作和表演上极其精彩的一笔。

151
00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.560
And I loved it.
我当时特别喜欢。

152
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.500
Just brilliant.
简直太棒了。

153
00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:15.860
Yeah, that was great.
是啊，那段真的很棒。

154
00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.360
I don't think we started with that.
我不觉得我们一开始就是这么设定的。

155
00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:23.000
I feel like we got to that eventually that it was going to be Jim that, that blew it.
我感觉我们最终决定让吉姆来搞砸这一切。

156
00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:33.720
Um, I can't remember exactly how that, uh, uh, started, but, um, yeah, no, it was great because you were expecting Michael to do it the whole time.
嗯，我不记得具体是怎么开始的了，但，嗯，对，没错，这很棒，因为观众一直以为会是迈克尔搞砸的。

157
00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.360
Yeah.
没错。

158
00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:41.860
And he, I just rewatched it this morning and God, John was so funny blowing it in the, in his, uh, toaSt.
而且他，我今天早上刚重温了一遍，天哪，约翰在祝酒词里搞砸的那段真是太搞笑了。

159
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.540
So good.
太精彩了。

160
00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.840
Cause he was doing so well up to there too.
因为在那之前他表现得一直很好。

161
00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.400
He was really killing it.
他当时发挥得太出色了。

162
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:54.620
Well, and then they have that great exchange where, um, where Michael says, this really takes the pressure off of me.
还有他们之间那段精彩的对话，迈克尔说，这真的减轻了我的压力。

163
00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:54.920
Yeah.
是啊。

164
00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.160
Like, this is great.
就像是，这太好了。

165
00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.920
Jim's like, I can't believe it was me.
吉姆说，我真不敢相信竟然是我。

166
00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.820
And Michael's like, I can't believe it either.
迈克尔说，我也不敢相信。

167
00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:01.540
Yeah.
是啊。

168
00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:01.900
Yeah.
没错。

169
00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:02.520
That was great.
那段太棒了。

170
00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.780
I mean, there was some, there was some great act breaks, right?
我是说，当时有一些非常棒的幕间节点，对吧？

171
00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.360
So we needed to have like six, six act breaks or something.
我们需要有六个左右的幕间节点。

172
00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:15.200
And another huge, huge thing was the act break of Jim and Pam running away.
另一个非常重大的节点是吉姆和帕姆私奔的那一段。

173
00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:19.340
Cause that was, that was pretty big too.
因为那段也相当重要。

174
00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:24.960
That felt like a romantic comedy to me that moment, you know, it really did.
那一刻给我的感觉就像浪漫喜剧一样，真的。

175
00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:29.520
It, it was so just everything, the lighting and they ran away.
一切都恰到好处，灯光，还有他们奔跑的样子。

176
00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:33.020
And then I love that you then see Meredith smoking the cigar.
然后我特别喜欢紧接着看到梅雷迪思抽雪茄的镜头。

177
00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.880
It's just this, this like beautiful moment.
那简直是一个非常美好的瞬间。

178
00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.380
And then there's Meredith, you know?
然后梅雷迪思就出现了，你懂的？

179
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:43.220
Well, speaking of romantic comedy, you wrote this episode with Mindy Kaling.
说到浪漫喜剧，这一集是你和敏迪·卡灵一起写的。

180
00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:43.700
Yeah.
没错。

181
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.640
You guys were nominated for an Emmy for this episode.
你们俩还凭借这一集获得了艾美奖提名。

182
00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.740
How did it come about that you guys wrote this together?
你们是怎么想到要一起写这一集的？

183
00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.020
Well, you know, it's interesting.
嗯，这很有趣。

184
00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:57.160
Mindy is such a lover of romantic comedy and I'm not a hundred percent sure.
敏迪非常热爱浪漫喜剧，我不太确定具体细节。

185
00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:02.060
I kind of feel like I had identified that she ought to write it.
我感觉当时是我认定她应该来写这一集。

186
00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:10.640
And then I was giving so many specific suggestions that there was this feeling of, well, you got a really strong feeling of how you want it to go.
然后我提出了很多具体的建议，以至于大家觉得，既然你对剧情走向有这么强烈的想法，

187
00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:11.940
Maybe you should co-write it.
也许你应该参与合写。

188
00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:15.040
So I feel like I came into it that way.
所以我感觉我是以这种方式加入的。

189
00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:21.500
And of course, you know, so many of the beats were coming from these cards that we had generated as a team.
当然，很多剧情点都来自我们团队一起构思的卡片。

190
00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:26.820
I mean, in re-reading the table draft, I was loving the first half so much.
重读剧本初稿时，我非常喜欢前半部分。

191
00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:30.420
I feel like that must have probably been her, her stuff.
我觉得那部分大概率是她写的。

192
00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:36.980
Because I have to take responsibility for Roy and the horse.
因为我得为罗伊和马的那段剧情负责。

193
00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:37.780
Okay.
好吧。

194
00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:38.320
Please.
请讲。

195
00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:38.880
Okay.
好的。

196
00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.480
How do we even set it up?
我们该怎么铺垫呢？

197
00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.740
Roy and the horse and the falls.
关于罗伊、马和瀑布的那段。

198
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.440
Greg, you have to tell the whole story.
格雷格，你得把整个故事讲出来。

199
00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:45.000
Right.
好的。

200
00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:53.860
Well, like I said, you know, so much of it was balancing how much comedy to put in and how much joy to put in.
就像我说的，很大程度上是在平衡喜剧成分和欢乐氛围的比例。

201
00:12:53.980 --> 00:13:05.620
And definitely I wanted to have that theme of there's all these things going wrong in the wedding, but Pam and Jim managed to carve out this beautiful private moment anyway.
我确实想表达这样一个主题：婚礼上虽然状况百出，但帕姆和吉姆还是设法创造了一个美好的私密时刻。

202
00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:06.160
Right.
没错。

203
00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:06.700
Right.
对。

204
00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:16.820
So the table draft had an act break where to top off all of these things that had been going wrong, like finding out about the pregnancy and.
所以剧本初稿里有一个幕间休息，为了给所有这些糟糕的事情画上句号，比如得知怀孕的消息，还有……

205
00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.100
Andy's scrotum, Michael and Pam's mom.
安迪的阴囊，迈克尔和帕姆的妈妈。

206
00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.120
Yeah, that was positive.
是啊，那段挺积极的。

207
00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:31.040
But to top it all off, like Roy shows up on a horse to try and make a grand gesture of take me back.
但最绝的是，罗伊骑着马出现，试图上演一出“回心转意”的宏大戏码。

208
00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.440
And it's just goes terribly.
结果简直糟透了。

209
00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:42.100
And, you know, this was a card that we had on the board, you know, early on about, you know, like those things, when those things happen in romantic comedy movies,
你知道，我们在白板上早就有过这样一个点子，就是那种浪漫喜剧电影里常有的桥段，

210
00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:43.020
they usually work.
通常这种招数都能奏效。

211
00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:47.660
And how awkward is it when it doesn't work and nobody wanted it and nobody was rooting for it.
但如果行不通，而且没人想要、也没人支持，那该有多尴尬啊。

212
00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:51.780
And, you know, you have to just ride your horse away.
然后你只能骑着马灰溜溜地走掉。

213
00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:56.300
And in the table draft, Greg, Roy rides in the church.
在剧本初稿里，格雷格，罗伊是骑马闯进教堂的。

214
00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:00.260
Jim is saying to have and to hold in sickness and in health.
当时吉姆正说着“无论疾病还是健康，都将不离不弃”。

215
00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:03.700
And there's like an audible like, and there's Roy on a horse.
然后现场传来一阵惊呼，罗伊就骑着马出现了。

216
00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:04.260
Yeah.
是啊。

217
00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.320
And Pam really is like, I don't, I don't want this.
帕姆当时的反应真的是：我不要，我才不想要这个。

218
00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.500
No, she had no intereSt.
没错，她一点兴趣都没有。

219
00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.280
I'm picking the man I love.
我选的是我爱的男人。

220
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.620
And I guess, thank you.
我想说，谢谢你。

221
00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.580
But can you turn your horse around?
但你能把马调头吗？

222
00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:15.420
Yeah.
没错。

223
00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:21.160
So, but I think what, what it was in that script was, it was ordered differently.
所以，我觉得那个剧本里的安排顺序不太一样。

224
00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.720
It was like, everything goes wrong at the wedding.
大概是婚礼上一切都乱套了。

225
00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:28.160
And then, and Michael's having the worst day.
迈克尔也过得极其糟糕。

226
00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:33.400
And then Jim gets the idea, I'm going to take Pam away and do it right.
然后吉姆想到了主意，我要带帕姆离开，去把婚礼办得完美。

227
00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:33.450
Right.
对。

228
00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.700
And he leaves Michael in charge.
于是他把迈克尔留下来负责。

229
00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:39.740
And then, and then there was in the script, there were like sort of two montages.
然后剧本里还有两段蒙太奇。

230
00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.520
There was the montage of Jim and Pam getting married on the Maid of the MiSt.
一段是吉姆和帕姆在“雾中少女号”上结婚的蒙太奇。

231
00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:49.260
And then there was the montage of Michael kind of killing it as being put in charge of the party.
另一段是迈克尔负责派对时大获成功的蒙太奇。

232
00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:50.460
And.
然后……

233
00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.060
Oh, right.
哦，对。

234
00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:56.400
Because they got married in the church first in the table draft.
因为在剧本初稿里，他们先在教堂结了一次婚。

235
00:14:56.640 --> 00:15:01.600
And then they have a second wedding while everybody else is at the reception.
然后在其他人参加招待会的时候，他们又办了第二次婚礼。

236
00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:02.340
Yeah.
是啊。

237
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:02.940
Yeah.
没错。

238
00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:17.560
I have to mention the other part about the horse, which was, there was a runner in that version where Dwight was fascinated being at Niagara Falls about the, the 1800s and the,
我必须提一下关于马的另一个部分，那个版本里有个贯穿始终的梗，德怀特对尼亚加拉大瀑布非常着迷，尤其是关于19世纪的历史，还有……

239
00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:23.480
and the history of people going over the falls in a barrel and animals surviving going over the falls.
人们坐木桶冲下瀑布的历史，以及动物在冲下瀑布后幸存下来的故事。

240
00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.180
Yes.
没错。

241
00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.880
In a way that, that people couldn't.
以一种人类无法做到的方式。

242
00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:35.060
And so after, after Roy does this whole thing, Dwight sees a free horse and decides he's going to test this out.
所以罗伊闹完那一出后，德怀特看到一匹没人管的马，决定亲自测试一下。

243
00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:46.100
And he takes the horse into the river and then he starts to getting swept towards the falls and he panics and he has to be rescued, but the horse goes over the falls, you know.
他把马带进河里，然后马开始被冲向瀑布，他惊慌失措不得不获救，但那匹马冲下了瀑布，你知道的。

244
00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:47.820
And then at the end, the horse is okay.
最后，那匹马没事。

245
00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:51.160
He's swimming away from the falls because he survived like some animals do.
它正从瀑布下游游走，因为它像某些动物一样幸存了下来。

246
00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:58.120
But you would have seen him as Jim and Pam are doing their second romantic wedding on Maid of the MiSt.
但当吉姆和帕姆在“雾中少女号”上举行第二次浪漫婚礼时，你会看到它。

247
00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:03.900
You were supposed to see it like a tiny horse going over, over the falls behind.
本来的设计是，你会看到背景里有一匹小小的马冲下了瀑布。

248
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.180
Yeah.
是啊。

249
00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:04.760
Yeah.
没错。

250
00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:05.620
That was the concept.
这就是那个构思。

251
00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.640
So anyway, so we read it at the table.
总之，我们在围读会上读了剧本。

252
00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.420
There was an awful lot of comedy in the script.
剧本里有很多喜剧元素。

253
00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:22.480
And I think we had just sort of over stacked the comedy and understacked the joy and the, you know, cause there was just too much bad things happening to poor Pam and Jim.
我觉得我们当时有点过度堆砌喜剧，而忽略了欢乐的部分，你知道，因为帕姆和吉姆身上发生的倒霉事太多了。

254
00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:28.580
And they had their great moment on the Maid of the Mist still, but everything that was public was kind of a disaster.
虽然他们依然在“雾中少女号”游船上有很棒的时刻，但除此之外的所有公开场合几乎都是一场灾难。

255
00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:37.240
And I think there was this very smart feeling from, you know, everybody, especially cast that, that was not cool.
我觉得大家，尤其是演员们，都敏锐地感觉到那样处理不太好。

256
00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:43.520
Like you got to give them more joy, the, the, the amount of the emotional balance and the episode was off.
就像是，你得给他们更多欢乐，那一集的情感平衡完全失调了。

257
00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:49.200
And also I, I think the cast that was all, you know, they were all friends and there,
而且我觉得演员们，你知道，他们私下都是朋友，而且，

258
00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:59.040
we had done so many episodes of them sort of turning into a family that it was, you just didn't want to be that negative and play them all as problems for Pam and Jim.
我们已经拍了那么多集，他们就像一家人一样，你真的不想表现得那么消极，把他们所有人都写成帕姆和吉姆的麻烦。

259
00:16:59.180 --> 00:16:59.260
Right.
没错。

260
00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:04.880
So that was sort of the message after the table read, but I, I was still producing.
所以这就是围读会后的共识，但我当时还在负责制片。

261
00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:14.380
And I remember going to scout the tank at Universal where the horse was going to be filmed in the water.
我记得当时去环球影城的片场勘景，那是打算拍摄马匹在水里戏份的地方。

262
00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.360
Cause that was like a big deal.
因为那可是个大工程。

263
00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:25.680
And like, I knew that we had to fix this, but I was still having to produce, you know, the version until, until it got changed.
我知道我们必须做出调整，但在方案修改之前，我还是得继续推进原定的制作。

264
00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:38.100
And, and, and I came back from that and Paul luckily had, had pulled this other card that we had had about, you know, the,
