为了捕捉所有这些声音，再加上他们为《尼亚加拉瀑布（上）》所需的一切，格雷格

701
00:40:56.280 --> 00:41:02.100
shared that they used the shorter opening title sequence because it saved us nine seconds,
分享说他们使用了较短的片头，因为这能为我们节省九秒钟，

702
00:41:02.100 --> 00:41:04.580
and we needed every single one of those.
而我们每一秒都需要。

703
00:41:05.080 --> 00:41:07.400
Well, I think we should get into this episode.
好吧，我觉得我们该进入这一集了。

704
00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:08.820
Let's do it.
开始吧。

705
00:41:09.020 --> 00:41:14.080
Well, let's start off right away with a deleted scene, Jenna.
那么，我们直接从一个删减片段开始吧，珍娜。

706
00:41:14.500 --> 00:41:15.000
Oh!
哦！

707
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:23.240
This episode would have started with Pam doing a wedding vlog at home as her and Jim got ready.
这一集原本是以帕姆在家录制婚礼视频博客作为开场的，当时她和吉姆正在准备。

708
00:41:23.240 --> 00:41:24.480
It's so adorable.
太可爱了。

709
00:41:24.740 --> 00:41:25.840
We have to hear it.
我们一定要听听。

710
00:41:26.840 --> 00:41:27.740
Hello, world.
你好，世界。

711
00:41:28.120 --> 00:41:33.340
This is Pam Beasley, and this is the latest installment of my wedding video diary.
我是帕姆·比斯利，这是我婚礼视频日记的最新一期。

712
00:41:34.480 --> 00:41:41.160
This afternoon, my fiancée Jim and I are going to Niagara Falls to get married after a half day of work.
今天下午，我和未婚夫吉姆要去尼亚加拉大瀑布结婚，在那之前还要上半天班。

713
00:41:42.420 --> 00:41:43.300
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

714
00:41:46.150 --> 00:41:47.850
Sorry, I'm just really excited.
抱歉，我只是太兴奋了。

715
00:41:48.470 --> 00:41:50.190
Okay, so let's see.
好吧，让我们看看。

716
00:41:50.930 --> 00:41:56.330
Last time I talked about the difficulties of throwing a wedding on a budget, specifically flower arrangements.
上次我谈到了预算有限时筹办婚礼的困难，特别是花艺布置方面。

717
00:41:57.170 --> 00:41:58.050
My solution?
我的解决方案？

718
00:41:59.630 --> 00:42:00.450
Paper flowers.
纸花。

719
00:42:01.330 --> 00:42:04.750
I made these using a regular cardstock that I found in the warehouse.
我用在仓库里找到的普通卡纸做的这些花。

720
00:42:05.190 --> 00:42:07.010
Can you believe they were going to just throw that away?
你能相信他们原本打算直接把这些扔掉吗？

721
00:42:09.320 --> 00:42:09.900
Hey, babe.
嘿，宝贝。

722
00:42:10.320 --> 00:42:10.660
Hey, babe.
嘿，宝贝。

723
00:42:11.220 --> 00:42:12.560
You gotta let me know when you're doing that.
你录的时候得告诉我一声。

724
00:42:13.480 --> 00:42:15.760
Okay, so I totally remember shooting these.
好的，我完全记得拍摄这些片段的情景。

725
00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:24.020
What is happening in the background there is that at the end of her vlog, Jim walks out of the bathroom in his underwear brushing his teeth.
背景里发生的事情是，在她视频博客的结尾，吉姆穿着内裤刷着牙从浴室走出来。

726
00:42:25.220 --> 00:42:27.860
And then he has to turn around and go back to the bathroom.
然后他不得不转身回到浴室。

727
00:42:28.180 --> 00:42:30.340
Yeah, he didn't know she was vlogging.
是的，他不知道她在录视频博客。

728
00:42:31.560 --> 00:42:39.420
They built a little, like, bedroom for Jim and Pam back behind where we would usually have lunch, a little bit off of our set.
他们在我们平时吃午饭的地方后面搭建了一个小小的卧室，就在我们片场旁边一点点。

729
00:42:39.520 --> 00:42:42.860
And we filmed these little vlogs in that little room.
我们就在那个小房间里拍摄了这些小视频。

730
00:42:43.180 --> 00:42:44.640
Well, they're super cute.
嗯，它们超级可爱。

731
00:42:44.640 --> 00:42:45.660
I loved them.
我很喜欢它们。

732
00:42:46.060 --> 00:42:46.540
Aw.
噢。

733
00:42:46.540 --> 00:42:54.560
Well, this episode actually gets started with Pam and Jim arriving to work in their cute little casual clothes.
那么，这一集实际上是从帕姆和吉姆穿着可爱的休闲装来上班开始的。

734
00:42:54.720 --> 00:42:58.920
And Michael is showing them how he has decorated his car for their wedding.
迈克尔正在向他们展示他为他们的婚礼装饰的车。

735
00:42:59.180 --> 00:43:00.040
His car.
他的车。

736
00:43:00.260 --> 00:43:01.020
His car.
他的车。

737
00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:05.080
His car is decorated and has cans behind it.
他的车装饰过了，后面还拖着罐子。

738
00:43:05.280 --> 00:43:05.660
Yes.
是的。

739
00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:11.240
Instead of saying just married on the back windshield, he wrote going to a wedding.
他没有在后挡风玻璃上写“新婚燕尔”，而是写了“去参加婚礼”。

740
00:43:14.860 --> 00:43:20.920
Well, Jim and Pam are going to ask everyone to come in the conference room because they want to give them a list of do's and don'ts for the wedding.
吉姆和帕姆要请大家到会议室，因为他们想给大家一份婚礼的注意事项清单。

741
00:43:21.400 --> 00:43:30.420
Already on the dry erase board, under the don'ts is make a big scene, cry, talk to our family, dash, very busy.
白板上已经写好了，在“不要”那一栏下写着：大吵大闹、哭泣、和我们的家人搭话——非常忙。

742
00:43:31.160 --> 00:43:36.060
Under the do's, it's have a good time, dance when it is appropriate.
在“要”那一栏下写着：玩得开心、在适当的时候跳舞。

743
00:43:36.740 --> 00:43:37.940
I liked that one.
我喜欢那一条。

744
00:43:38.220 --> 00:43:39.220
And eat dinner.
还有吃晚饭。

745
00:43:39.920 --> 00:43:44.520
Right away, there's a heated debate because Kevin, I guess, really wanted to bring firecrackers.
紧接着就发生了一场激烈的争论，因为凯文，我想，他真的很想带鞭炮来。

746
00:43:44.820 --> 00:43:45.000
Yeah.
是的。

747
00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:47.500
So Jim has to put that under the don't column.
所以吉姆不得不把它写在“不要”那一栏下。

748
00:43:47.680 --> 00:43:53.320
And now here comes the big secret they really need everyone to not say with them.
现在，他们真正需要大家保密的大秘密来了。

749
00:43:53.780 --> 00:43:55.580
Do not say Pam is pregnant.
不要说帕姆怀孕了。

750
00:43:55.820 --> 00:43:56.600
Don't do it.
千万别说。

751
00:43:56.760 --> 00:43:57.580
Don't say it.
别说出来。

752
00:43:58.340 --> 00:44:00.100
Pam's meemaw doesn't know.
帕姆的奶奶还不知道呢。

753
00:44:00.580 --> 00:44:01.520
Don't say it.
别说出来。

754
00:44:02.020 --> 00:44:04.600
Angela tells Pam she's lucky to have a grandmother.
安吉拉告诉帕姆，她能有位奶奶真是幸运。

755
00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:09.720
Jenna, this is one of my lines from the whole run of the show that gets quoted to me.
珍娜，这是整部剧里我被引用最多的一句台词。

756
00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:12.880
I'll be at Target and someone will say it to me.
我逛塔吉特百货时，总有人跟我说这句话。

757
00:44:13.240 --> 00:44:15.160
Well, you're lucky you have a grandmother.
好吧，你有奶奶真是幸运。

758
00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:17.180
Some of us have to be our own grandmothers.
我们有些人只能自己当自己的奶奶。

759
00:44:17.840 --> 00:44:18.100
Hmm.
嗯。

760
00:44:18.980 --> 00:44:19.400
Yeah.
是啊。

761
00:44:19.620 --> 00:44:22.100
I think Angela Martin and Meemaw would have hit it off.
我觉得安吉拉·马丁和奶奶应该会很投缘。

762
00:44:22.380 --> 00:44:25.680
Oh, I so wish we could have had an Angela Meemaw scene.
噢，我真希望我们能拍一场安吉拉和奶奶的对手戏。

763
00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:26.440
I know.
我也这么想。

764
00:44:26.440 --> 00:44:29.640
Why weren't they seated side by side at the rehearsal dinner?
她们在彩排晚宴上为什么没坐在一起呢？

765
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:30.920
No kidding.
可不是嘛。

766
00:44:31.260 --> 00:44:32.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

767
00:44:32.960 --> 00:44:36.900
Well, Pam sort of retorts to Angela, you know, you don't have to come to the wedding.
帕姆算是回击了安吉拉，你知道的，说她不必非得参加婚礼。

768
00:44:37.060 --> 00:44:38.260
And Michael's like, yes, she does.
迈克尔就说，不，她必须参加。

769
00:44:38.560 --> 00:44:41.140
And he leans forward and he pinches Angela.
然后他身体前倾，掐了安吉拉一下。

770
00:44:42.100 --> 00:44:43.620
Jenna, Steve really pinched me.
珍娜，史蒂夫是真的掐了我。

771
00:44:43.780 --> 00:44:45.420
And that reaction is real.
那个反应是真实的。

772
00:44:45.540 --> 00:44:46.500
I really went, ow!
我当时真的喊了声“哎哟”！

773
00:44:48.020 --> 00:44:51.280
Was that in the script or was that just like a little thing he did?
那是剧本里写的，还是他自己临时加的小动作？

774
00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:54.860
No, it was scripted that Michael pinches Angela under her arm.
不，剧本里写了迈克尔要掐安吉拉的胳膊下面。

775
00:44:54.860 --> 00:44:59.120
But you guys, when was the last time someone pinched you like under your arm?
但各位，你们有多久没被人掐过胳膊下面了？

776
00:44:59.860 --> 00:45:02.580
You have an honest reaction when it happens.
那种事发生时，你的反应绝对是真实的。

777
00:45:03.220 --> 00:45:03.740
Sure.
确实。

778
00:45:04.540 --> 00:45:08.000
Well, Michael and Dwight are hoping a lot happens at this wedding.
迈克尔和德怀特指望着在这场婚礼上发生点什么。

779
00:45:08.360 --> 00:45:10.080
Oh, yeah, they are.
噢，没错，他们确实指望着呢。

780
00:45:10.440 --> 00:45:15.520
You know, in traditional Dwight and Michael style, there was a deleted scene, Jenna, where
你知道，按照德怀特和迈克尔的一贯风格，有一个删减片段，珍娜，是

781
00:45:15.520 --> 00:45:17.040
Dwight helps Michael pack.
德怀特帮迈克尔打包行李。

782
00:45:17.280 --> 00:45:18.300
He goes over the liSt.
他核对清单。

783
00:45:18.460 --> 00:45:19.240
You know how he does.
你知道他那套作风。

784
00:45:20.080 --> 00:45:23.620
Jenna, Michael shares that he's going to bring 78 iteMs.
珍娜，迈克尔说他要带78件物品。

785
00:45:23.620 --> 00:45:26.880
You need to hear what these 78 items are.
你得听听这78件物品都是什么。

786
00:45:27.040 --> 00:45:27.860
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

787
00:45:28.980 --> 00:45:30.580
Deodorant, toothpaste, check.
除臭剂，牙膏，检查完毕。

788
00:45:32.750 --> 00:45:34.430
Yes, extra large.
没错，超大号的。

789
00:45:34.630 --> 00:45:36.150
I brought 78 condoMs.
我带了78个避孕套。

790
00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:37.150
Oh, man.
天呐。

791
00:45:38.330 --> 00:45:39.370
78, Jenna.
78个，珍娜。

792
00:45:40.090 --> 00:45:40.530
Wow.
哇。

793
00:45:40.950 --> 00:45:41.350
Yeah.
是啊。

794
00:45:42.270 --> 00:45:42.370
Hmm.
嗯。

795
00:45:42.930 --> 00:45:43.050
Hmm.
嗯。

796
00:45:43.690 --> 00:45:49.390
Dwight has made a list of every one of Jim and Pam's female family members and is going
德怀特列了一份名单，上面有吉姆和帕姆所有的女性家属，他打算

797
00:45:49.390 --> 00:45:51.650
to break down their eligibility, sort of.
分析一下她们的单身状况，算是吧。

798
00:45:51.650 --> 00:45:59.050
Well, if you count whether or not they've sold their bicycle online as a dating status.
如果你把她们是否在网上卖过自行车也算作一种恋爱状态的话。

799
00:45:59.530 --> 00:46:00.650
Yeah, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

800
00:46:01.010 --> 00:46:05.750
You know, we got a fan question from Lauren Kay in Canada that I really appreciated.
你知道，我们收到了一位来自加拿大劳伦·凯的粉丝提问，我非常喜欢。

801
00:46:06.210 --> 00:46:11.230
She said, I've never understood why everyone is always at the office before they go to leave
她说，我一直不明白为什么大家在离开去某地之前，总要先到办公室一趟，

802
00:46:11.230 --> 00:46:14.090
somewhere, similar to, like, when Holly moved.
就像霍莉搬走时那样。

803
00:46:14.270 --> 00:46:14.650
Oh.
哦。

804
00:46:14.890 --> 00:46:17.590
Or before Pam went off to New York City.
或者在帕姆去纽约之前也是。

805
00:46:18.090 --> 00:46:21.610
Why are Jim and Pam at the office the day before their wedding?
为什么吉姆和帕姆在婚礼前一天还要来办公室？

806
00:46:21.870 --> 00:46:26.310
Why is anyone there if they're just going to all leave in their casual clothes anyway?
既然他们反正都要换上便装离开，为什么还要来呢？

807
00:46:26.910 --> 00:46:29.350
You know, Lauren, I don't know.
你知道吗，劳伦，我也不知道。

808
00:46:29.510 --> 00:46:32.510
I don't know what work they got done today.
我不知道他们今天在办公室到底做了什么工作。

809
00:46:32.850 --> 00:46:36.030
Perhaps Jim and Pam needed to come in to give everyone this speech.
也许吉姆和帕姆需要过来给大伙儿发表这番演讲。

810
00:46:36.030 --> 00:46:40.770
They saw the value in that one last speech to the group about Meemaw.
他们觉得在临走前对大家讲讲米玛的事很有意义。

811
00:46:41.250 --> 00:46:42.470
But I agree.
但我同意你的看法。

812
00:46:42.470 --> 00:46:43.650
I think it's very funny.
我觉得这确实挺逗的。

813
00:46:43.990 --> 00:46:48.710
I'm just glad that Pam isn't driving to her wedding in a pencil skirt with pantyhose.
我只是庆幸帕姆不用穿着铅笔裙和连裤袜去参加自己的婚礼。

814
00:46:49.050 --> 00:46:49.650
Finally.
终于不用了。

815
00:46:50.090 --> 00:46:53.570
Well, now everybody's going to kind of get in their little carpools.
好了，现在大家都要各自去拼车了。

816
00:46:53.850 --> 00:46:57.830
Michael and Dwight drive off in his decorated car.
迈克尔和德怀特开着那辆装饰过的车离开了。

817
00:46:58.170 --> 00:46:59.750
The cans are exploding.
罐头在不断爆炸。

818
00:47:00.630 --> 00:47:02.870
We got a fan question about that as well.
我们正好也收到了一个关于此事的粉丝提问。

819
00:47:03.670 --> 00:47:04.050
John D.
来自科罗拉多州莱克伍德的约翰·D。

820
00:47:04.170 --> 00:47:06.790
from Lakewood, Colorado said, how did they do that?
问，他们是怎么做到的？

821
00:47:07.070 --> 00:47:07.950
Was it real?
那是真的吗？

822
00:47:08.070 --> 00:47:08.990
Was it special effects?
还是特效？

823
00:47:09.470 --> 00:47:11.070
I mean, the cans were real.
我是说，罐头本身是真的。

824
00:47:11.330 --> 00:47:14.430
I guess this gag drove the crew crazy.
我猜这个恶作剧把剧组折腾坏了。

825
00:47:14.730 --> 00:47:18.930
Randy, Kelly, and Veda shared that it was just a very difficult thing to get.
兰迪、凯利和维达分享说，这其实非常难拍。

826
00:47:19.030 --> 00:47:21.370
It seems like a small little moment, right, in the script?
在剧本里这看起来只是个小插曲，对吧？

827
00:47:21.570 --> 00:47:23.210
But it was very hard to capture.
但要拍出来却非常困难。

828
00:47:23.210 --> 00:47:31.230
Yeah, Randy told me that the writers were so tickled by this idea that these cans would explode.
没错，兰迪告诉我，编剧们对“罐头会爆炸”这个点子感到非常兴奋。

829
00:47:31.430 --> 00:47:34.070
That Michael would put full cans, you guys.
迈克尔竟然放了装满东西的罐头，伙计们。

830
00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:35.690
You're supposed to put empty cans.
本来应该放空罐头的。

831
00:47:35.850 --> 00:47:35.990
Yes.
没错。

832
00:47:36.070 --> 00:47:37.530
But Michael wouldn't think that through.
但迈克尔根本没考虑过这一点。

833
00:47:37.990 --> 00:47:44.650
They started by just dragging some full cans behind the car, hoping they would explode.
他们一开始只是试着在车后拖着几个满罐头，希望能让它们炸开。

834
00:47:44.650 --> 00:47:45.650
They didn't.
结果没炸。

835
00:47:45.650 --> 00:47:53.890
So they actually had to rig each can with a teeny tiny timed explosive charge to make them burst open.
所以他们不得不给每个罐头都装上微型定时炸药，好让它们爆开。

836
00:47:54.510 --> 00:47:55.490
That happened.
确实发生了。

837
00:47:55.610 --> 00:47:57.950
They burst open, but it wasn't all that exciting.
它们爆开了，但看起来没那么震撼。

838
00:47:57.950 --> 00:48:03.490
So then they also had to add like a sound effect to make it sort of louder.
所以他们还得加上音效，让声音听起来响一点。

839
00:48:03.810 --> 00:48:07.290
It was a very difficult little bit to pull off.
这确实是个很难完成的小片段。

840
00:48:08.050 --> 00:48:12.010
But listen, this is a tradition, the thing of putting cans on the back of your car.
不过听着，在车后挂罐头这可是个传统。

841
00:48:12.010 --> 00:48:13.830
Of course, I looked it up.
当然，我查过了。

842
00:48:13.970 --> 00:48:19.190
I guess that this goes all the way back to a French tradition, Angela.
我猜这可以追溯到一个法国传统，安吉拉。

843
00:48:19.510 --> 00:48:19.830
Oh.
哦。

844
00:48:20.090 --> 00:48:24.470
It's called, I'm going to pronounce this wrong, chivalry.
它叫——我发音可能会错——“喧闹仪式”（charivari）。

845
00:48:25.810 --> 00:48:32.010
And you're supposed to like create a bunch of noise after a couple is newly married.
据说在新婚夫妇结婚后，人们要制造出一大堆噪音。

846
00:48:32.550 --> 00:48:40.090
It was originally done where as the couple drove away, people would clang pots and pans and other noisemakers.
最初的做法是，当新人开车离开时，人们会敲打锅碗瓢盆和其他能发出声响的东西。

847
00:48:40.090 --> 00:48:42.930
But then it eventually evolved into the can thing.
后来才演变成了挂罐头的习俗。

848
00:48:43.490 --> 00:48:45.670
But I thought you'd like this one, Angela.
但我猜你会喜欢这个，安吉拉。

849
00:48:45.990 --> 00:48:49.070
I guess in the Tudor period in England.
我猜是在英国的都铎王朝时期。

850
00:48:49.430 --> 00:48:52.210
I was going to say, how far back does this go?
我正想问，这习俗到底有多久远了？

851
00:48:52.590 --> 00:48:52.850
Yeah.
没错。

852
00:48:53.150 --> 00:49:03.330
There was this crazy tradition where as the couple would ride away in their carriage, guests would take off their shoes and throw them at the carriage.
过去有个疯狂的传统，当新婚夫妇坐马车离开时，宾客们会脱下鞋子朝马车扔过去。

853
00:49:04.110 --> 00:49:06.890
And if you hit the carriage, it meant good luck.
如果你扔中了马车，就意味着好运。

854
00:49:06.890 --> 00:49:12.730
So, there have always been these little traditions of things to do as a couple is driving away.
所以，一直以来都有各种各样的小传统，是在新人驱车离开时做的。

855
00:49:13.330 --> 00:49:14.970
Throwing things at them.
往他们身上扔东西。

856
00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:16.270
Clanking noise.
叮当声。

857
00:49:16.850 --> 00:49:17.010
Yeah.
没错。

858
00:49:18.230 --> 00:49:21.190
But that stunt was a nightmare.
但那个特技简直是场噩梦。

859
00:49:22.090 --> 00:49:24.390
I have a driving stunt coming up.
我接下来有个开车特技。

860
00:49:24.570 --> 00:49:25.550
Yes, you do.
没错，确实有。

861
00:49:25.810 --> 00:49:27.110
You're going to run into Kevin.
你要撞上凯文了。

862
00:49:27.670 --> 00:49:31.850
I fully nudge Brian Baumgartner with that car, you guys.
伙计们，我真的用那辆车轻轻撞了布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳一下。

863
00:49:31.990 --> 00:49:33.270
And it was a lot of fun.
而且那真的很有趣。

864
00:49:33.270 --> 00:49:36.790
And listen, I was going 0.000 miles an hour.
听着，我当时的时速是0.000英里。

865
00:49:36.910 --> 00:49:37.610
It was just a little tap.
只是轻轻碰了一下。

866
00:49:37.750 --> 00:49:38.370
Just a little tap.
就轻轻碰了一下。

867
00:49:38.830 --> 00:49:40.810
And we actually had a lot of fun doing that.
我们拍那段戏其实玩得很开心。

868
00:49:40.910 --> 00:49:41.830
I got really tickled.
我当时真的被逗乐了。

869
00:49:42.930 --> 00:49:44.450
Everyone's on their way to Niagara now.
现在大家都已经在去尼亚加拉的路上了。

870
00:49:44.610 --> 00:49:46.270
You have all these different pairings and cars.
车里有各种不同的组合。

871
00:49:46.270 --> 00:49:47.230
It's really fun to see.
看起来真的很有趣。

872
00:49:47.390 --> 00:49:48.750
You have Andy, Aaron, and Kelly.
有安迪、亚伦和凯莉。

873
00:49:49.190 --> 00:49:52.050
And you have Jim and Pam and Michael and Dwight.
还有吉姆和帕姆，以及迈克尔和德怀特。

874
00:49:52.510 --> 00:49:52.850
Yes.
没错。

875
00:49:53.230 --> 00:49:56.030
There's that super sweet scene with Pam and Jim.
帕姆和吉姆那场戏超级温馨。

876
00:49:56.030 --> 00:49:59.790
And this is where we get, oh my gosh, I just loved it.
这就是我们看到的，天哪，我真是太喜欢了。

877
00:50:00.450 --> 00:50:06.750
Pam tells Jim that her aunt told her to take mental pictures of the high points of their wedding day
帕姆告诉吉姆，她姑妈让她把婚礼当天的美好瞬间拍成“心理照片”记在脑海里，

878
00:50:06.750 --> 00:50:10.250
because everything's going to go by so fast and they should try to remember it.
因为一切都会过得很快，他们应该试着记住这些时刻。

879
00:50:10.450 --> 00:50:15.550
And that's when Jim uses his fingers and pretends like he's taking a picture of Pam.
然后吉姆就用手指假装在给帕姆拍照。

880
00:50:16.090 --> 00:50:20.750
This idea that Jim and Pam should take mental pictures was a pitch from Steve Carell.
吉姆和帕姆要拍“心理照片”这个点子是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔提出来的。

881
00:50:20.750 --> 00:50:26.090
He had told Greg this story that he had a friend who would do this.
他告诉格雷格，他有个朋友以前就会这么做。

882
00:50:26.330 --> 00:50:29.570
And so Greg put it into the script for Jim and Pam.
于是格雷格就把这个情节写进了吉姆和帕姆的剧本里。

883
00:50:29.770 --> 00:50:33.810
But when we read it, John and I, we didn't get it like when we read the script.
但当我们读剧本的时候，我和约翰并没有完全理解。

884
00:50:34.330 --> 00:50:37.130
So Greg did that thing where he was like, Steve, come here, come here.
所以格雷格就做了那种事，他说：“史蒂夫，过来，过来。”

885
00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:38.570
Show these guys what you meant.
“给他们演示一下你是什么意思。”

886
00:50:38.650 --> 00:50:40.290
The thing with the taking the mental pictures.
就是拍“心理照片”那件事。

887
00:50:40.510 --> 00:50:42.250
So Steve kind of showed us.
于是史蒂夫给我们演示了一下。

888
00:50:42.650 --> 00:50:45.110
And then we were like, oh, we get it.
然后我们就说，哦，我们懂了。

889
00:50:45.430 --> 00:50:46.690
I just love that so much.
我真的太喜欢那个瞬间了。

890
00:50:46.770 --> 00:50:49.610
And it goes to what Greg mentioned in the commentary, you guys.
这正如格雷格在评论音轨里提到的，伙计们。

891
00:50:49.610 --> 00:50:56.730
And also in our interview about how a lot of this episode was based off real life moments in people's lives.
还有我们在采访中也聊过，这一集里的很多内容都是基于人们生活中的真实瞬间。

892
00:50:56.890 --> 00:50:57.730
And this is one of them.
而这就是其中之一。

893
00:50:57.930 --> 00:51:00.830
You know, I also improvised a line in the scene, Angela.
你知道吗，安吉拉，那场戏里还有一句台词是我即兴发挥的。

894
00:51:01.110 --> 00:51:01.790
Which line?
哪一句？

895
00:51:03.370 --> 00:51:06.290
When Jim says, oh, you blinked.
当吉姆说，哦，你眨眼了。

896
00:51:06.470 --> 00:51:08.230
That was supposed to be the end.
那本来应该是结尾的。

897
00:51:08.570 --> 00:51:10.410
And I improvised the line.
然后我即兴加了一句台词。

898
00:51:10.570 --> 00:51:13.370
We should have hired a professional to take our mental pictures.
我们应该雇个专业摄影师来帮我们拍心理照片的。

899
00:51:13.770 --> 00:51:15.970
Oh, I'm very proud of it.
哦，我对此感到非常自豪。

900
00:51:16.130 --> 00:51:17.030
Very good.
非常好。

901
00:51:18.010 --> 00:51:21.550
So Angela, you mentioned that Dwight and Michael are in the car together.
安吉拉，你提到德怀特和迈克尔在一起开车。

902
00:51:21.630 --> 00:51:30.730
And I laughed out loud so hard at the beginning of the scene when you find out that Michael is asleep and driving.
当发现迈克尔在睡觉开车时，那个场景的开头让我笑得前仰后合。

903
00:51:31.190 --> 00:51:31.550
Yeah.
没错。

904
00:51:31.990 --> 00:51:33.450
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

905
00:51:33.710 --> 00:51:43.510
I also laughed out loud when Dwight says he made Michael a mix CD, something he can play if he brings a woman back to his room.
当德怀特说他给迈克尔做了一张混音CD，让他带女人回房间时可以放，我也笑出了声。

906
00:51:43.510 --> 00:51:45.950
I mean, Dwight is a wingman, guys.
我是说，德怀特真是个僚机，伙计们。

907
00:51:46.330 --> 00:51:48.330
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

908
00:51:48.330 --> 00:51:50.090
I felt like we needed to hear it.
我觉得我们得听听看。

909
00:51:51.330 --> 00:51:51.490
Hello.
你好。

910
00:51:52.010 --> 00:51:53.490
My name is Dwight Schrute.
我叫德怀特·舒鲁特。

911
00:51:53.730 --> 00:51:57.910
If you are listening to this, you're a lucky woman Michael has seduced.
如果你正在听这个，那你就是迈克尔诱惑成功的幸运女人。

912
00:51:58.110 --> 00:51:59.990
Ah, to be in your shoes.
啊，真羡慕你。

913
00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:02.370
What's next, you're probably wondering.
你可能在想，接下来该怎么办。

914
00:52:02.670 --> 00:52:05.290
Don't be scared of your night in heaven.
别害怕你这如天堂般的夜晚。

915
00:52:07.750 --> 00:52:10.710
I mean, it's so creepy.
我是说，这太毛骨悚然了。

916
00:52:11.610 --> 00:52:12.930
Maximum creep factor.
恐怖指数爆表。

917
00:52:13.430 --> 00:52:16.830
This scene made me laugh for something I was not expecting, Jenna.
珍娜，这个场景让我笑的原因是我没想到的。

918
00:52:17.450 --> 00:52:17.890
What?
什么？

919
00:52:19.230 --> 00:52:21.650
I couldn't stop cracking up.
我笑得停不下来。

920
00:52:21.790 --> 00:52:22.430
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

921
00:52:22.570 --> 00:52:23.930
Maybe I was just in a loopy mood.
也许我当时只是有点神志不清。

922
00:52:24.250 --> 00:52:26.610
I don't know if it was intentional or not.
我不知道这是否是有意为之。

923
00:52:26.610 --> 00:52:30.590
But did you notice that Michael is dressed just like his car seat?
但你注意到迈克尔穿得和他的车座一模一样了吗？

924
00:52:31.250 --> 00:52:31.410
What?
什么？

925
00:52:31.710 --> 00:52:34.790
He's dressed exactly like the upholstery in his car.
他穿得和车里的内饰完全一样。

926
00:52:35.130 --> 00:52:38.150
So he's in all beige and the seat is all beige.
他穿了一身米色，车座也是全米色的。

927
00:52:38.290 --> 00:52:41.490
And he's just like a beige blob going down the road.
他就像一团米色的东西在路上移动。

928
00:52:41.630 --> 00:52:43.590
And it just cracked me up.
这真的让我笑喷了。

929
00:52:43.970 --> 00:52:46.570
I did not, but I want to go back and look at it.
我没注意到，但我得回去看看。

930
00:52:47.050 --> 00:52:50.130
Well, you guys, the gang finally makes it to Niagara.
好了，伙计们，大家终于到了尼亚加拉。

931
00:52:50.350 --> 00:52:51.630
They're pulling into the city.
他们正驶入这座城市。

932
00:52:51.630 --> 00:52:56.610
For that driving sequence as everyone arrives to Niagara, Kelly Cantley shared,
关于大家到达尼亚加拉的那段驾驶镜头，凯利·坎特利分享说，

933
00:52:56.790 --> 00:53:00.930
that was filmed, Jenna, while you guys were drying off from Maid of the MiSt.
珍娜，那是你们在“雾中少女号”游船上弄干身体时拍摄的。

934
00:53:01.330 --> 00:53:02.370
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

935
00:53:02.370 --> 00:53:02.890
Yeah.
是的。

936
00:53:03.330 --> 00:53:07.790
For the most part, we shot this episode in Los Angeles.
这一集大部分是在洛杉矶拍摄的。

937
00:53:08.090 --> 00:53:14.690
And all of the scenes at the hotel were shot at Sportsman's Lodge in Studio City.
酒店的所有场景都是在影城的运动员旅馆拍摄的。

938
00:53:15.570 --> 00:53:19.690
For the lobby area, we used an area that was under renovation,
大堂区域我们用的是一个正在翻修的区域，

939
00:53:19.690 --> 00:53:21.550
that was kind of in the back of the hotel.
就在酒店后面。

940
00:53:22.110 --> 00:53:26.390
Our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, and our set decorator, Steve Rothstein,
我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格和布景师史蒂夫·罗斯坦，

941
00:53:27.210 --> 00:53:34.010
they basically turned this unused lobby into this fictitious Statler Falls Hotel.
他们基本上把这个闲置的大堂改造成了虚构的斯塔特勒瀑布酒店。

942
00:53:34.570 --> 00:53:36.030
What an amazing job.
真是了不起的工作。

943
00:53:36.210 --> 00:53:40.170
I mean, everything from like the fireplace, all of it that you see, they put in there.
我是说，从壁炉到你看到的一切，都是他们放进去的。

944
00:53:40.710 --> 00:53:41.190
Everything.
所有的一切。

945
00:53:41.550 --> 00:53:45.330
All the hotel rooms, they were upstairs on the second floor.
所有的酒店房间都在二楼。

946
00:53:45.330 --> 00:53:49.450
It was an unused wing of the hotel that was undergoing a renovation at the time.
那是酒店当时正在翻修的一处闲置侧翼。

947
00:53:49.690 --> 00:53:50.710
They were empty.
它们都是空的。

948
00:53:50.970 --> 00:53:56.670
So literally, everything you see was added by our design crews, which I just think is amazing.
所以从字面上看，你看到的一切都是我们的设计团队添加的，我觉得这太神奇了。

949
00:53:57.410 --> 00:54:03.570
And lady, do you remember when we talked to Ed Helms about when he started on the office,
还有，女士，你还记得我们和艾德·赫尔姆斯聊到他刚加入《办公室》时，

950
00:54:03.750 --> 00:54:06.970
he stayed at Sportsman's Lodge?
他住在运动员旅馆的事吗？

951
00:54:07.190 --> 00:54:08.670
Yeah, that's where they put him up.
没错，他们就是把他安排在那儿。

952
00:54:08.830 --> 00:54:09.390
Yes.
是的。

953
00:54:10.290 --> 00:54:16.310
Because, incidentally, when Lee and I got married, Sportsman's Lodge was down the street from our house.
顺便提一下，因为李和我结婚的时候，Sportsman's Lodge 就在我们家那条街上。

954
00:54:16.850 --> 00:54:21.110
And we found out that you could buy a day pass for their swimming pool.
我们发现可以买他们游泳池的日票。

955
00:54:21.270 --> 00:54:25.030
They have a huge swimming pool, like an Olympic-sized swimming pool.
他们有一个巨大的游泳池，就像奥林匹克标准泳池那么大。

956
00:54:25.530 --> 00:54:32.090
And so whenever my family would come to town, we would get day passes for the Sportsman's Lodge swimming pool.
所以每当我的家人来城里时，我们都会去买 Sportsman's Lodge 游泳池的日票。

957
00:54:32.090 --> 00:54:35.010
Jenna, my dad loved the Sportsman's Lodge.
珍娜，我爸爸很喜欢 Sportsman's Lodge。

958
00:54:35.370 --> 00:54:37.890
We would go there and swim and hang out.
我们会去那里游泳和消磨时光。

959
00:54:37.990 --> 00:54:42.090
And you and I often met there for breakfast because they had a fantastic breakfaSt.
而且你和我经常在那里见面吃早餐，因为他们的早餐棒极了。

960
00:54:42.470 --> 00:54:45.550
They had an amazing little breakfast diner restaurant thing.
他们有一个很棒的小型早餐餐厅。

961
00:54:46.050 --> 00:54:53.630
Well, Randy also shared with me that we had to do a table read for one of our upcoming episodes while we were shooting at Sportsman's Lodge.
兰迪还跟我说，我们在 Sportsman's Lodge 拍摄期间，还得为即将到来的一集进行剧本围读。

962
00:54:53.630 --> 00:55:00.510
And they put us in this conference room, but it had a huge window right onto the swimming pool.
他们把我们安排在一个会议室里，但那儿有一扇巨大的窗户正对着游泳池。

963
00:55:00.650 --> 00:55:02.590
He said we got a lot of looky-loos.
他说我们引来了很多围观群众。

964
00:55:02.750 --> 00:55:08.930
A lot of people, like, in their bathing suits and towels, just, like, walking by watching us read an episode of The Office.
很多人穿着泳衣、裹着浴巾，就那样走过，看着我们围读《办公室》的剧本。

965
00:55:09.270 --> 00:55:15.910
Also, try concentrating on reading and delivering a line as, like, some guy is chasing after a beach ball.
而且，试着在有人追着沙滩球跑的时候，集中注意力去阅读和念台词吧。

966
00:55:16.210 --> 00:55:16.650
Yeah.
没错。

967
00:55:16.850 --> 00:55:17.890
In his swim trunks.
还穿着泳裤。

968
00:55:18.350 --> 00:55:21.370
Well, now Jim and Pam are going to check in to their hotel room.
好了，现在吉姆和帕姆要去办理酒店入住手续了。

969
00:55:21.370 --> 00:55:25.630
And I want you guys to look at 8 minutes, 41 seconds.
我想让大家看 8 分 41 秒处。

970
00:55:26.190 --> 00:55:33.330
There is a beautiful photo, a huge picture in the lobby of Niagara Falls, of the actual falls.
大堂里有一张漂亮的照片，一张尼亚加拉大瀑布的巨幅照片，就是瀑布本尊。

971
00:55:33.710 --> 00:55:36.910
Well, that was taken by our very own Michael Gallenberg.
那是我们自己的迈克尔·加伦伯格拍的。

972
00:55:37.210 --> 00:55:39.150
Randy and Michael had gone there to scout.
兰迪和迈克尔曾去那里踩点。

973
00:55:39.150 --> 00:55:44.910
And on their scouting trip, Michael took that picture and blew it up really big and made it part of the lobby decoration.
在踩点期间，迈克尔拍下了那张照片，把它放得很大，并让它成为了大堂装饰的一部分。

974
00:55:45.430 --> 00:55:46.930
Oh, I love that detail.
哦，我喜欢这个细节。

975
00:55:46.930 --> 00:55:51.510
Now, during this scene, Jim and Pam make it clear that they're going to get individual rooms tonight.
在这一幕中，吉姆和帕姆明确表示他们今晚要住单独的房间。

976
00:55:51.590 --> 00:55:54.530
And then the next night, they're going to check into the honeymoon suite.
然后第二天晚上，他们才去办理蜜月套房的入住。

977
00:55:54.770 --> 00:55:57.290
But they're wondering, like, can we just take a peek at it?
但他们想，我们能先去瞄一眼吗？

978
00:55:57.350 --> 00:55:58.510
We just want to look at it.
我们只是想看一眼。

979
00:55:58.810 --> 00:56:01.630
And the hotel desk clerk is like, oh, I'm sorry.
酒店前台职员说，哦，抱歉。

980
00:56:01.990 --> 00:56:03.470
Someone has that room tonight.
今晚有人住那间房。

981
00:56:03.870 --> 00:56:05.450
And that someone is Andy.
而那个人就是安迪。

982
00:56:06.150 --> 00:56:08.630
Andy is staying in the honeymoon suite.
安迪住在蜜月套房里。

983
00:56:08.630 --> 00:56:10.030
The night before.
就在前一天晚上。

984
00:56:10.310 --> 00:56:12.410
And he's like, I'll break it in for you guys.
他说，我会帮你们先“暖暖房”的。

985
00:56:13.050 --> 00:56:14.250
John delivers this line.
约翰念了这句台词。

986
00:56:14.390 --> 00:56:15.150
It was in the script.
剧本里就是这么写的。

987
00:56:15.330 --> 00:56:17.710
I had to look it up because the way he did it was so funny.
我特意去查了一下，因为他演绎的方式太搞笑了。

988
00:56:17.810 --> 00:56:19.750
I thought maybe he made it up on the fly.
我还以为是他即兴发挥的呢。

989
00:56:19.950 --> 00:56:22.410
He just says, I do not like that.
他只是说，我不喜欢那样。

990
00:56:23.810 --> 00:56:24.910
I do not like that.
我不喜欢那样。

991
00:56:25.290 --> 00:56:26.350
It's so great.
太棒了。

992
00:56:26.990 --> 00:56:30.990
Well, listen, I have a guest star alert that is near and dear to my heart.
听着，我有一个非常特别的客串明星提醒，这对我意义重大。

993
00:56:30.990 --> 00:56:37.750
The woman who plays the front desk clerk throughout this episode is my friend Michelle Gunn.
在这一集中饰演前台职员的女士是我的朋友米歇尔·冈恩。

994
00:56:38.270 --> 00:56:40.990
Now, I have known Michelle for so long.
我和米歇尔认识很久了。

995
00:56:41.030 --> 00:56:48.650
And she auditioned for The Office six times for six different roles before landing this one.
她在拿到这个角色之前，曾为《办公室》试镜过六次，竞争过六个不同的角色。

996
00:56:48.850 --> 00:56:49.770
I didn't know that.
我不知道这件事。

997
00:56:50.270 --> 00:56:50.870
Yes.
是的。

998
00:56:51.050 --> 00:56:55.370
And she would get to the final callbacks and then they'd give the role to someone else.
她总是能进入最终复试，但最后角色还是给了别人。

999
00:56:55.510 --> 00:56:57.610
But Alison Jones kept bringing her back.
但艾莉森·琼斯一直让她回来试镜。

1000
00:56:57.830 --> 00:57:00.890
We would always be so bummed when she didn't get a role.
每当她没拿到角色时，我们总是感到非常沮丧。

1001
00:57:00.990 --> 00:57:06.910
But then she got this huge role where she got to interact with almost every cast member.
但后来她得到了一个非常重要的角色，几乎能和剧组里的每一位成员演对手戏。

1002
00:57:06.910 --> 00:57:09.450
She got to be directed by Paul Feig.
她还得到了保罗·费格的执导。

1003
00:57:09.590 --> 00:57:13.370
And she got paid for two different episodes.
而且她拿到了两集戏份的片酬。

1004
00:57:13.690 --> 00:57:15.310
So we were so excited.
所以我们当时特别兴奋。

1005
00:57:15.450 --> 00:57:20.490
We were like, oh my gosh, this is that story where like every job you didn't get
我们当时就觉得，天哪，这就是那种“你没得到的每一份工作，

1006
00:57:20.490 --> 00:57:23.710
leads to the job you absolutely were meant to have.
最终都会引向你命中注定的那份工作”的故事。

1007
00:57:23.850 --> 00:57:24.950
How fun.
真有意思。

1008
00:57:25.270 --> 00:57:26.670
And she's so good in it.
而且她在里面的表现太棒了。

1009
00:57:26.770 --> 00:57:27.650
She's so good.
她演得太好了。

1010
00:57:27.870 --> 00:57:28.830
Oh, she crushed it.
噢，她简直演绝了。

1011
00:57:28.830 --> 00:57:33.230
I want you to know, I noticed a background catch in this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，我想让你知道，我在这场戏里发现了一个背景细节。

1012
00:57:33.530 --> 00:57:34.810
It's really quick.
一闪而过的那种。

1013
00:57:34.990 --> 00:57:35.550
What you got?
你发现了什么？

1014
00:57:36.070 --> 00:57:36.450
Okay.
好。

1015
00:57:36.890 --> 00:57:43.790
There is like a little announcement board that sort of says all the other things that are
有个小公告板，上面写着那天晚上酒店里

1016
00:57:43.790 --> 00:57:45.890
happening at the hotel on this night.
正在进行的所有其他活动。

1017
00:57:45.990 --> 00:57:47.070
Oh, what's it say?
噢，上面写了什么？

1018
00:57:47.070 --> 00:57:47.890
All right.
好吧。

1019
00:57:48.190 --> 00:57:51.210
I live for this, by the way, and I'm sad I missed it.
顺便说一下，我最爱这种细节了，没能亲自发现真遗憾。

1020
00:57:51.330 --> 00:57:52.550
So I cannot wait to hear.
所以我迫不及待想听听了。

1021
00:57:52.890 --> 00:57:59.130
Well, in addition to Jim and Pam's rehearsal dinner, you could also attend the Moose Lodge
嗯，除了吉姆和帕姆的彩排晚宴，你还可以参加晚上7点在麋鹿厅举行的

1022
00:57:59.130 --> 00:58:00.550
meeting at 7 p.m.
驼鹿小屋会议。

1023
00:58:00.590 --> 00:58:01.330
in the Elk Room.
在麋鹿厅。

1024
00:58:02.510 --> 00:58:06.270
Or Senior Poker Friday at 5 p.m.
或者下午5点在河厅举行的老年人扑克周五活动。

1025
00:58:06.370 --> 00:58:07.290
in the River Room.
在河厅。

1026
00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:12.490
Or perhaps you'd like to go to the O'Brien Retirement Party at 8 p.m.
又或者你可能想去参加晚上8点在接待大厅举行的奥布莱恩退休派对。

1027
00:58:12.490 --> 00:58:14.150
in the Reception Hall.
在接待大厅。

1028
00:58:15.030 --> 00:58:17.190
I also noticed this tidbit.
我还注意到了这个小花絮。

1029
00:58:17.550 --> 00:58:22.750
I know exactly when Jim and Pam's wedding reception is because it's on the board.
我知道吉姆和帕姆的婚宴确切时间，因为板子上写着。

1030
00:58:22.750 --> 00:58:24.190
It's 2 p.m.
是下午2点。

1031
00:58:24.490 --> 00:58:26.450
the next day in the Falls Room.
第二天在瀑布厅。

1032
00:58:26.450 --> 00:58:29.730
So they had like, I guess, like a noon-ish wedding.
所以我想，他们的婚礼大概是在中午左右举行的。

1033
00:58:30.450 --> 00:58:34.170
Well, someone's going to get some bad news when they try to check into the hotel, and
好吧，当迈克尔试图办理入住时，他肯定会听到坏消息，

1034
00:58:34.170 --> 00:58:38.810
that person is Michael because I guess he thought you could just show up and say you
因为他大概以为只要直接过去说他想要一间比斯利-哈珀特预留区的房间，

1035
00:58:38.810 --> 00:58:41.550
want a room with the Beasley Halpert block.
就能拿到房间。

1036
00:58:41.870 --> 00:58:43.250
And you would have a room.
他以为就能有房间住。

1037
00:58:43.630 --> 00:58:45.090
That's not how it works.
事情可不是这么运作的。

1038
00:58:45.270 --> 00:58:45.890
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1039
00:58:46.590 --> 00:58:50.490
So Michael's going to try to weasel himself into other people's rooMs.
所以迈克尔打算厚着脸皮挤进别人的房间。

1040
00:58:50.930 --> 00:58:53.090
Of course no one wants Michael in their room.
当然，没人想让迈克尔住进自己的房间。

1041
00:58:53.090 --> 00:58:57.710
The only person who's nice enough to say, Michael, you could have the other bed is Toby.
唯一好心说“迈克尔，你可以睡另一张床”的人是托比。

1042
00:58:58.030 --> 00:58:59.990
And Michael's like, um, hell no, Toby.
而迈克尔的反应是：呃，想都别想，托比。

1043
00:59:00.490 --> 00:59:01.510
I know.
我知道。

1044
00:59:02.170 --> 00:59:07.070
You know, Stanley's going to arrive to check in with not his wife.
你知道，斯坦利来办理入住时带的不是他妻子。

1045
00:59:07.570 --> 00:59:08.130
Cynthia.
是辛西娅。

1046
00:59:09.030 --> 00:59:09.590
Cynthia.
辛西娅。

1047
00:59:10.790 --> 00:59:13.350
Played by Algerita Wynne Lewis.
由阿尔杰里塔·韦恩·刘易斯饰演。

1048
00:59:14.150 --> 00:59:15.590
This is a bit scandalous.
这可是有点丑闻性质了。

1049
00:59:15.910 --> 00:59:18.870
I'm surprised Angela didn't have something to say about this.
我很惊讶安吉拉竟然没对此发表什么评论。

1050
00:59:19.210 --> 00:59:22.710
Angela was consumed with the fact that Pam was getting married while pregnant.
安吉拉当时满脑子想的都是帕姆怀孕结婚的事。

1051
00:59:22.710 --> 00:59:24.630
She could barely focus on anything else.
她几乎无法专注于其他任何事情。

1052
00:59:25.050 --> 00:59:25.850
That's right.
没错。

1053
00:59:26.030 --> 00:59:28.710
She was focusing all her shame in that one direction.
她把所有的羞耻感都集中在那一个方向上。

1054
00:59:29.970 --> 00:59:37.210
I love that Michael goes up to Jim and Pam and asks when is he making his speech and says,
我喜欢迈克尔走到吉姆和帕姆面前，问他什么时候致辞，然后说，

1055
00:59:37.310 --> 00:59:39.130
because he'd like to go third to bat cleanup.
因为他想第三个上场，来个压轴。

1056
00:59:39.890 --> 00:59:40.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1057
00:59:40.570 --> 00:59:43.530
This is where we are going to meet Jim's parents for the first time.
这就是我们要第一次见到吉姆父母的地方。

1058
00:59:44.130 --> 00:59:49.610
We have Betsy Halpert, played by Perry Smith, and Gerald Halpert, played by Robert Pine,
贝琪·哈珀特由佩里·史密斯饰演，杰拉德·哈珀特由罗伯特·派恩饰演，

1059
00:59:49.610 --> 00:59:52.350
who is the father of actor Chris Pine.
他就是演员克里斯·派恩的父亲。

1060
00:59:52.950 --> 00:59:54.270
People were so excited.
大家当时都非常兴奋。

1061
00:59:54.770 --> 00:59:56.350
We were a little bit excited.
我们也有点兴奋。

1062
00:59:56.790 --> 01:00:00.110
First of all, he's a lovely, lovely person and was so nice to everyone.
首先，他是一个非常非常可爱的人，对每个人都很好。

1063
01:00:00.110 --> 01:00:03.250
But there were a few folks excited that Chris Pine's dad was there.
但确实有几个人因为克里斯·派恩的爸爸在场而感到兴奋。

1064
01:00:03.530 --> 01:00:04.290
It's true.
这是真的。

1065
01:00:04.530 --> 01:00:08.490
Even though Robert Pine is like an incredibly successful actor in his own right.
尽管罗伯特·派恩本身就是一位非常成功的演员。

1066
01:00:08.490 --> 01:00:18.350
Well, listen, Pam and Jim are pointing out Meemaw to Jim's parents, and she says,
听着，帕姆和吉姆向吉姆的父母指着米玛，她说，

1067
01:00:18.650 --> 01:00:21.370
Meemaw is the woman in teal talking to my mom.
米玛就是那个穿着蓝绿色衣服、正在和我妈妈说话的女人。

1068
01:00:21.810 --> 01:00:27.790
Now, that was confusing to some viewers because, you know, we met Pam's mom in the sexual harassment
这让一些观众感到困惑，因为你知道，我们在第二季的“性骚扰”

1069
01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:29.070
episode in season two.
那一集中见过帕姆的妈妈。

1070
01:00:29.070 --> 01:00:35.450
And the woman that we met as Pam's mom was not standing over by the woman in teal.
而我们当时见到的那个帕姆的妈妈，并没有站在那个穿蓝绿色衣服的女人旁边。

1071
01:00:35.770 --> 01:00:40.010
Because in this episode, Pam has a new mom.
因为在这一集里，帕姆换了个新妈妈。

1072
01:00:40.270 --> 01:00:43.710
We had to cast a new actress as Pam's mom.
我们不得不为帕姆的妈妈选了一位新演员。

1073
01:00:44.090 --> 01:00:44.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1074
01:00:45.250 --> 01:00:48.970
The original actress who played Pam's mom was Shannon Cochran.
饰演帕姆妈妈的原版演员是香农·科克伦。

1075
01:00:49.550 --> 01:00:52.670
She was on tour doing a play.
她当时正在巡回演出一部话剧。

1076
01:00:52.890 --> 01:00:54.530
She was doing August Osage County.
她在演《八月：奥色治郡》。

1077
01:00:54.750 --> 01:00:56.930
And we could not get her for this episode.
我们没能请到她来拍这一集。

1078
01:00:57.470 --> 01:00:59.070
Randy actually talked about this.
兰迪其实谈到过这件事。

1079
01:00:59.230 --> 01:01:05.570
He said this was a really difficult episode to schedule because we had so many different
他说这一集的拍摄档期非常难排，因为我们有太多不同的

1080
01:01:05.570 --> 01:01:09.790
guest stars, many of whom we had established in previous episodes.
客串明星，其中许多人我们在之前的剧集中已经设定好了。

1081
01:01:09.790 --> 01:01:11.330
We had to get the same people.
我们必须请到同一个人。

1082
01:01:12.130 --> 01:01:14.650
We even had to shoot on two Saturdays.
我们甚至不得不连续两个周六进行拍摄。

1083
01:01:14.750 --> 01:01:16.030
I don't know if you remember that, Angela.
安吉拉，我不知道你还记不记得。

1084
01:01:16.310 --> 01:01:21.870
But in order to get everybody in the same room together for the wedding part, we actually
但为了让所有人都能在婚礼那场戏里聚在一起，我们确实

1085
01:01:21.870 --> 01:01:23.070
shot on Saturdays.
在周六进行了拍摄。

1086
01:01:23.190 --> 01:01:25.150
The one person we couldn't get was Shannon.
唯一没能请到的人就是香农。

1087
01:01:25.150 --> 01:01:27.530
Again, the writers talked about this.
编剧们再次谈到了这一点。

1088
01:01:27.910 --> 01:01:30.890
They felt that we had to have Pam's mom at the wedding.
他们觉得帕姆的妈妈必须出现在婚礼上。

1089
01:01:31.110 --> 01:01:31.570
They did not.
他们不想那样做。

1090
01:01:32.090 --> 01:01:34.250
Like, Pam couldn't get married without her mom.
就像是，帕姆不可能在没有妈妈的情况下结婚。

1091
01:01:34.530 --> 01:01:35.010
No.
没错。

1092
01:01:35.310 --> 01:01:40.490
They did not want to manufacture some kind of drama like that Pam's mom didn't come.
他们不想编造出那种帕姆的妈妈没来参加婚礼的戏剧冲突。

1093
01:01:40.830 --> 01:01:41.290
Right.
对。

1094
01:01:41.590 --> 01:01:47.450
Plus, they really wanted to introduce that storyline between Michael and Pam's mom.
另外，他们真的很想引入迈克尔和帕姆妈妈之间的那条故事线。

1095
01:01:48.610 --> 01:01:51.510
And that was an important storyline for this season.
那对这一季来说是一条重要的故事线。

1096
01:01:51.830 --> 01:01:56.810
And it looked like Shannon's tour schedule was going to bump into that as well.
而且看起来香农的巡演档期也会和那条线冲突。

1097
01:01:56.970 --> 01:02:00.290
So they made the decision to recast the role.
所以他们决定重新选角。

1098
01:02:00.810 --> 01:02:03.130
Pam's new mom was played by Linda Pearl.
帕姆的新妈妈由琳达·珀尔饰演。

1099
01:02:03.550 --> 01:02:06.410
When I met her, I was really struck with how alike we look.
当我见到她时，我真的很惊讶我们长得有多像。

1100
01:02:06.590 --> 01:02:11.650
It's funny because the original actress, Shannon, kind of looks like my real mom.
很有趣，因为最初的演员香农，长得有点像我现实中的妈妈。

1101
01:02:11.650 --> 01:02:14.870
But I thought Linda looked kind of like me.
但我以为琳达长得有点像我。

1102
01:02:15.110 --> 01:02:18.210
I actually thought she looked like she could be my big sister.
我其实觉得她长得像我姐姐。

1103
01:02:19.130 --> 01:02:20.970
And we were doing the math.
我们当时还算了算。

1104
01:02:20.990 --> 01:02:24.890
And we were like, wait, actually, like, we're not that far apart in age.
我们心想，等等，其实我们年龄差得并不大。

1105
01:02:25.010 --> 01:02:27.450
Like, she would have been 19 when she had me.
她生我的时候才19岁。

1106
01:02:27.810 --> 01:02:29.430
A little bit of Hollywood magic there.
这算是好莱坞的一点小魔力吧。

1107
01:02:29.610 --> 01:02:30.290
A little fudging.
稍微动了点手脚。

1108
01:02:30.470 --> 01:02:32.730
They tried to play it up with, like, her hair, makeup, wardrobe.
他们试图通过发型、妆容和服装来强化这种感觉。

1109
01:02:32.730 --> 01:02:34.570
But here's something crazy.
但有件疯狂的事。

1110
01:02:34.570 --> 01:02:36.310
She's been acting for forever.
她演戏演了很久了。

1111
01:02:36.650 --> 01:02:38.470
She had been on Happy Days.
她还演过《欢乐时光》。

1112
01:02:38.710 --> 01:02:40.190
How cool is that?
那多酷啊？

1113
01:02:40.510 --> 01:02:41.670
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

1114
01:02:42.310 --> 01:02:43.710
Well, Linda was delightful.
琳达真的很讨人喜欢。

1115
01:02:43.870 --> 01:02:45.990
I loved getting to work with her.
我非常喜欢和她合作。

1116
01:02:46.250 --> 01:02:52.130
At 11 minutes, 3 seconds, people are making their way into where the rehearsal dinner is.
在11分03秒处，人们正走进彩排晚宴的场地。

1117
01:02:52.310 --> 01:02:55.570
There is a sign that says Beasley Halpert.
那里有个牌子写着“比斯利-哈尔珀特”。

1118
01:02:56.230 --> 01:02:58.450
Now, Halpert is spelled wrong.
不过，哈尔珀特的拼写错了。

1119
01:02:59.010 --> 01:03:03.850
And some people on the internet at the time were like, oh, my gosh, they spelled Jim's last name wrong.
当时网上有些人说，天哪，他们把吉姆的姓拼错了。

1120
01:03:04.630 --> 01:03:06.770
Veda shared on the commentary, that was intentional.
维达在评论音轨里分享说，那是故意的。

1121
01:03:07.110 --> 01:03:13.250
That was like a little joke, a little hidden Jim, a little nugget, you know, that the hotel staff had spelled his name wrong.
那是个小玩笑，一个小彩蛋，你知道的，暗示酒店员工把他的名字拼错了。

1122
01:03:13.450 --> 01:03:14.950
So that was meant to be, you guys.
所以那是刻意为之的，伙计们。

1123
01:03:15.490 --> 01:03:22.910
Yes, Angela, on that little sign that I mentioned earlier, every time it's supposed to say Halpert, it says Halpert.
没错，安吉拉，在我刚才提到的那个小牌子上，每次应该写“哈尔珀特”的地方，都写成了“哈尔珀特”。

1124
01:03:23.290 --> 01:03:24.570
It's like a running joke.
这就像个连贯的笑话。

1125
01:03:24.670 --> 01:03:26.090
You can find many Halperts.
你能发现很多个“哈尔珀特”。

1126
01:03:26.090 --> 01:03:30.070
The other information on the sign reads like this.
牌子上的其他信息是这样的。

1127
01:03:30.370 --> 01:03:34.310
Wedding rehearsal dinner, 7 to 8.40 p.m.
婚礼彩排晚宴，晚上7点到8点40分。

1128
01:03:34.830 --> 01:03:36.410
Yeah, guys, you've got to get out.
没错，伙计们，你们得离开。

